      "question": {
        ":question/id": "372ef5b2-d4be-54dd-8cf1-89bb9cfee364",
        ":question/problem": "$\\int \\frac{8}{x+10}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, let $u=x+10.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,\u27f9\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can now rewrite the integral in terms of $u,$ solve it, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8}{x+10}\\,\\text{d}x & =8\\int \\frac{1}{x+10}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|u|+C \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|x+10|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
